  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The effective current <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi></math> in the given circuit at very high frequencies will be _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0066_ac9949967b54.png\" style=\"width: 450px; height: 179px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "44",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>At very high frequencies,&nbsp;inductor acts as an open circuit&nbsp;and capacitor as short circuit.</p><p>So, capacitive reactance,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>&omega;</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&asymp;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Also, inductive reactance,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>&omega;</mi><mi>L</mi><mo>&asymp;</mo><mo>&infin;</mo></math></p><p>Thus, equivalent circuit can be redrawn as</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0066_91ec30d938c1.png\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 147px;\" /></p><p>Here, both&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&Omega;</mi></math>&nbsp;resistances are in parallel and together they are in series with<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&Omega;</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&Omega;</mi></math>&nbsp;resistances.</p><p>Equivalent impedance is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>&times;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&Omega;</mi></math></p><p>Effective current is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>220</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&Omega;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>44</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
}